body: |-
  ## The Marathon Session

  What started as "let's make dealoracle work with the new orchestration" turned into building the complete Paradigm agent army over ~5 hours.

  ### Timeline

  1. **Conductor daily-driver** (v5.7.0) — global binary install, project discovery, resume UX, instance linking
  2. **Conductor help system** — 9-section in-app guide, sidebar + NxM grid layout rewrite
  3. **dealoracle migration** — paradigm shift, .purpose schema analysis, checkpoint crash fix (v5.8.1)
  4. **First 8 agents** — Mika, Scout, Wren, Atlas, Sage, Bolt, Helix, Loid + Yuki's PM agent from dealoracle
  5. **Paradigm enrichment** — architect (orchestration lead), security (portal champion), reviewer (compliance), Atlas (Sentinel master), plus Sage, Bolt, Helix, Yuki with Paradigm MCP knowledge
  6. **Creative/specialist wave** — Ghost (e2e), Pixel (gamedev), Prism (creative director), Neon (3D), Sheila (educator), Conduit (CLI/MCP builder), Sunday (personal secretary)
  7. **Generalist wave** — Jinx (devil's advocate), Trace (debugger), Ink (narrator), Compass (ethicist), Index (archivist), Bridge (mediator), Echo (audio), Root (sysadmin), Stage (presenter)
  8. **Business wave** — Mozi (Hormozi sales), Leila (operations/company building)
  9. **Final wave** — Beacon (SEO), Babel (i18n), Clause (legal), Shield (QA strategy), North (product), Vault (DBA), Obi (mentor), Horizon (futurist), Gather (community)
  10. **Specialist wave** — Sensei (agent trainer), Flux (streaming/WebRTC), Oracle (AI/ML), Swift (mobile), Aria (accessibility), Pipeline (data engineering), Ship (release manager), Wire (network protocols)
  11. **Intelligence + finance** — Lens (content extraction), Rosetta (translator), Cipher (reverse engineer), Ledger (finance)

  ### Notebook Bootstrapping

  269 entries distilled from canonical sources including:
  - Material Design 3 (10 entries — tonal palettes, shape, type, motion, components)
  - Apple HIG (10 entries — principles, safe areas, SF Symbols, Dynamic Type, visionOS, dark mode)
  - WCAG 2.2 (8 entries — contrast, focus, target size, reflow, text spacing, color independence)
  - Radix Colors (7 entries — 12-step scale, backgrounds, borders, alpha, dark mode, composition)
  - Tailwind CSS (8 entries — tokens, responsive, dark mode, container queries, spacing, typography)
  - OWASP Top 10 (4 entries — A01-A10 with prevention patterns)
  - Playwright (8 entries — locators, auto-waiting, fixtures, POM, visual regression, a11y, CI, traces)
  - Hormozi methodology (12+10 entries — value equation, Grand Slam Offers, CLOSER, Core Four, Leila's frameworks)
  - Color theory fundamentals (14 entries — wheel, spaces, oklch, psychology, temperature, dark mode theory)
  - Typography (6 entries — classification, modular scale, pairing, line height, variable fonts, heading hierarchy)
  - Iconography (3 entries — icon systems, design rules, accessibility)
  - Plus: Blender, Godot, Unity, Midjourney, Runway, spaced repetition, Bloom's taxonomy, MCP protocol, and more

  ### Architecture Decisions

  - **Pods** are a nevr.land platform feature, not agent behavior — derived from collaboration graphs
  - **7-tier taxonomy** organizes agents by function: Builders, Reviewers, Strategists, Intelligence, Infrastructure, Meta, Human Ops
  - **Notebook bootstrapping** is essential — agents need hard knowledge before their first session
  - **Named nicknames** create identity: "Ask Mika" > "run designer agent"

  ### What's Next

  - Field test orchestration with the full roster on dealoracle
  - Build Sensei's training loop — have him review agent performance and write targeted notebook entries
  - Begin nevr.land registry with these 54 as the official archetype collection
  - Design renaissance — Mika now has 59 entries of design knowledge, ready to lead the visual overhaul
